<title>PORTUGAL: Angolan airline TAAG buys SIA Boeing 747-300.</title>
<headline>Angolan airline TAAG buys SIA Boeing 747-300.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>TAAG-Angola Airlines has bought a Boeing 747-300 from Singapore Airlines ltd for use on existing international routes, the Angolan embassy in Lisbon said in a statement.</p>
<p>The plane, able to carry up to 270 passengers and 55 tonnes of cargo, will replace a Lockheed Tristar on lease from TAP-Air Portugal for the past six years, it said.</p>
<p>The Boeing will operate on the Lisbon-Luanda run amongst other routes, it added.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
